sequenceDiagram
  %% Development mail: install the private SMTP path and IPv4 loopback proxies.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:mail:update
  %% kind: instance.mail_update
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>Instance container
  CLI->>GW: instance:mail:update 42
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:mail:update INSTANCE`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance> [--json]`
  Note over GW: Admit mail update
  %%> When:
  %%> - only a development container on the Node running the main Mailpit; hold its Instance lock
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - unsupported placement or unfinished lifecycle work starts no run
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-mail-update
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation ID
  SW->>N: Apply mail path and listeners<br/>Ansible mail phase
  %%> When:
  %%> - refuse a stopped container; never start it
  %%> Why:
  %%> - one reusable step admits the exact SMTP endpoint, merges the own ACL rule, and installs two loopback socket proxies
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - retain applied state for an idempotent retry; do not touch the workspace or application Processes
  alt applied or unchanged
    N-->>SW: Mail path result<br/>applied · unchanged · skipped
    %%> When:
    %%> - a foreign listener or unit file skips setup with a named reason, without stopping the Project's Process
    SW-->>GW: Record mail result
  else phase failed
    N--xSW: Mail path failed
    SW--xGW: Record failure
  end
  loop until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show<br/>Operation ID
    GW-->>CLI: Status and result
  end
